**Go/No-Go Rule:** Failure of any gate reverts architecture to uncrewed precursor missions or delays crewed launch to next solar-max window (approximately 2043–2046 if 2032–2035 window is missed). The addition of the dust health gate and the fracture risk gate represents a tightening of the feasibility conditions relative to earlier analyses.

**Artemis schedule risk:** The original gate matrix assumed Artemis III surface operations in 2026. As of 2026, Artemis III has not launched. If Artemis III surface physiology data is not collected before 2028, the Mars conjunction-class BMD and fracture risk models will remain unvalidated at the time of any plausible 2033 crew launch decision gate. This represents the single highest-risk programmatic dependency in the entire Mars constraint budget.

