## 11. Synthesis: Feasible Envelope & Monte Carlo Comparison

### 11.1 Explicit Envelope Inequalities

The feasible mission region $\mathcal{F}$ is defined by the constrained optimization set, updated to include the fracture risk constraint, Mars dust erosion reliability term, and BNNT-LC shielding improvement:

$$\mathcal{F} = \left\{ \begin{aligned} & D_{\text{total}}(P_e, m_{\text{shield}}, t_{\text{EVA}}) \leq 600 \text{ mSv} \\ & P(\text{fracture}) < 0.05 \text{ per crew member per mission} \\ & m_{\text{launch}} = m_{\text{dry}} + \alpha_{\text{MARVL}} P_e + m_{\text{ISRU}} + m_{\text{shield}} + m_{\text{dust-health}} \leq 150 \text{ t} \\ & t_{\text{tr}} = \frac{\Delta v}{\sqrt{2 \eta P_e / m_{\text{dry}}}} \leq 180 \text{ d} \\ & P_e \geq 1 \text{ MWe}, \quad \omega \leq 2 \text{ rpm}, \quad \beta_{\text{Mars, mitigated}} \leq 0.08, \quad A(T) \geq 0.99 \\ & \epsilon_d(T_{\text{storm}}) \geq 0.3 \text{ (ISRU operational during storm season)} \end{aligned} \right\}$$

The feasible region exists only for $P_e \geq 1$ MWe, $m_{\text{shield}} \geq 20$ g/cm² BNNT-LC, solar-max trajectory alignment, Artemis-validated fracture risk countermeasures, and dust-mitigated system reliability.

### 11.2 Monte Carlo Scenario Comparison

| Scenario | Parameters | $P(D_{\text{total}} \leq 600 \text{ mSv})$ | $R_{\text{sys}}$ | Fracture Risk | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Case 1 (2033)** | Solar max, 1 MWe NEP, 20 g/cm² BNNT-LC, 2 m berm, 4 hr/day EVA, active dust mitigation | 74% | 0.91 | ~20% (with countermeasures) | **Viable with margin** |
| **Case 2 (2035)** | Solar min, 0.2 MWe NEP, 10 g/cm² Al, 0 m berm, 6 hr/day EVA, no dust mitigation | 1.8% | 0.74 | ~62% | **Non-viable** |
| **Case 3 (2033, new)** | Solar max, 1 MWe NEP, 20 g/cm² BNNT-LC, dust unmitigated | 74% | 0.31 | ~20% | **Non-viable (dust CCF collapse)** |

Case 3 is a new scenario illustrating the consequence of the revised dust erosion amplifier. Even with optimal propulsion and shielding, neglecting dust-driven common-cause failure drops $R_{\text{sys}}$ from 0.91 to 0.31 — actuarially unacceptable. This is the sharpest single addition to the constraint budget relative to prior analyses.

